						<div style="width:100%;">
							<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span style="font-size: 24pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">New Members <o:p></o:p></span></strong></p> <div class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span style="font-size: 24pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue; font-weight: normal;"> <hr align="center" size="2" width="100%" /> </span></strong></div> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">&nbsp;</span></p> <ul type="disc"> <li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">New members gain&nbsp;DKP just like established members. However, new members cannot vote on raid or guild bank items, until they have been with the guild for 30 days.<span style="">&nbsp; </span>(The exceptions to this rule are listed under the Rules and Regulations)</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">New members cannot become officers or raid looters during their 30-day probationary period. </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">If a person would like to join Moonlite Redemption, they can apply at the website by&nbsp;posting in the <a href="/forums/threadlist.aspx?fid=1691">Applications</a> forum.&nbsp;Tell us a little about yourself such as your character name, class and level, as well as why you would like to join MR, etc.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">We take characters of all races and classes. The minimum level requirement is 55, excluding alts. </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">An existing member must sponsor new members during their probationary period. The sponsor is responsible for reporting any misconduct to an officer, and making sure that new members understand the guild rules and regulations. </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Reports of misconduct may result in immediate removal. All probationary members are subject to removal with or without previous notification or reason. </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">All members need to make sure that the guild/site leader has their email address.&nbsp; The site email address is: moonlite_redemption@yahoo.com</span></li> </ul> <p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p> <p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Verdana; color: red;">Prerequisites for New Members </span></strong><strong><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;"><o:p></o:p></span></strong></p> <div class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: center;" align="center"><strong><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue; font-weight: normal;"> <hr align="center" size="2" width="100%" /> </span></strong></div> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">&nbsp;</span></p> <ul type="disc"> <li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">New members must be level 55 or above. This does not apply to current members' alternate characters. </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">A current member must sponsor new members, if a class officer is unable, a current member may be asked to sponsor that person.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"> <o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">New members must read and follow the<a href="../custom.aspx?pid=1035"> Rules and Regulations</a>.&nbsp; </span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">Applications will be reviewed and applicants will receive an answer either in game, email or via a reply to their post.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li class="MsoNormal" style=""><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">The recruiting officer or guild leaders, on a probationary status, will invite qualified applicants to the guild.</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana; color: blue;">One month after joining, the sponsor, class officers and guild leaders will discuss the new member and determine whether the member is ready for full membership.<span style="">&nbsp; </span>The member’s “joined date” will be removed from the guild manager when full membership is granted.</span></li> </ul> 
							
